The '''Aerospace Exploration Agency''' ({{lang-bl|Axencia de Exploracion Aeroespacial; '''AXA'''}}) is the {{W|aeronautics}} and {{W|space agency}} of the [[Baliscan Confederation]]. Its main facilities are located in [[Alcovadia]] ([[Bayara|Bayara)]], at the [[Maravíes Aerospace Center]]. AXA's stated vision is to continue building upon domestic launch capabilities, furthering international cooperation regarding the exploration of space, industrialize satellite information and applications technology, and develop more sustainable and highly-efficient cutting-edge aircraft and core aerospace technology.  

AXA cooperates extensively with the the space programs of [[Soviet Union]], {{W|China space program|China}}. Additionally, it works with the [[Baliscan Aerospace Force]], sharing the responsibility of the development and upkeep of the [[South American Navigation|SAN satellite navigation system]]. 

